{"name":"Black Squeeze","hex":"#e5e6df","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"squeeze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply pressure (to something) from two or more sides at once.","To embrace closely; to give a tight hug to."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of squeezing.","A close or tight fit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Squeeze (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Squeeze are an English rock band that came to prominence in the United Kingdom during the new wave period of the late 1970s, and continued recording in the 1980s, 1990s and 2010s. In the UK, their singles \"Cool for Cats\", \"Up the Junction\", and \"Labelled with Love\" were top-ten chart hits. Though not as commercially successful in the United States, Squeeze had American hits with \"Tempted\", \"Black Coffee in Bed\", and \"Hourglass\", and were considered a part of the Second British Invasion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Squeeze_2021-09-14.jpg/330px-Squeeze_2021-09-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squeeze_(band)"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Squeeze_1979.jpg/330px-Squeeze_1979.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Squeeze_1979.jpg/330px-Squeeze_1979.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The band in April 1979. Top: Jools Holland, middle (left to right): John Bentley, Chris Difford, Gilson Lavis, bottom row: Glenn Tilbrook.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASqueeze_1979.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/MoseleyFolk010923_%28112_of_121%29_%2853160386428%29.jpg/500px-MoseleyFolk010923_%28112_of_121%29_%2853160386428%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/MoseleyFolk010923_%28112_of_121%29_%2853160386428%29.jpg/1280px-MoseleyFolk010923_%28112_of_121%29_%2853160386428%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/MoseleyFolk010923_%28112_of_121%29_%2853160386428%29.jpg/500px-MoseleyFolk010923_%28112_of_121%29_%2853160386428%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Difford and Tilbrook in 2023","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoseleyFolk010923_(112_of_121)_(53160386428).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Squeeze_2020-02-26.jpg/500px-Squeeze_